# Publish and deploy after every finished task

The site is a test version that only the owner uses. Every finished change goes to `main` and is deployed to the production domain automatically, without asking for each publication. This replaces any earlier "do not publish to main" or "wait for deploy permission" instruction.

## Workflow

1. Implement the task.
2. Run the needed tests and a build check (for this repo: `npx tsx scripts/erp/test-erp.ts` for ERP changes, `npx tsc --noEmit -p .`, `npx next build`; not `npm run build`, its prebuild rewrites menu images in `public/menu`).
3. When the checks pass, bring the changes into `main` without losing anyone else's changes and without force-push.
4. Push `main` and wait for the Vercel deployment to succeed (`npx --no-install vercel` is logged in).
5. Open the affected page on https://www.gastrotruck.org and check that the new version is really there.
6. Report what was published, with a link to the page.

The task is finished only when the result is live on the site and checked after publication. Do not stop at a commit in a separate branch.

## Database migrations

- Compatible migrations that only add needed tables, columns, indexes or functions without losing data are applied as part of the task, before the code that needs them goes live.
- Deleting data, resetting the database, or any change that risks losing existing data needs the owner's separate approval.

## Rules

- If tests or the deployment fail, fix the cause. Never report a successful publication without confirmation.
- Commit only files related to the task. Never commit secrets (`.env`, `.env.local`) or unrelated files (for example other people's images in `food/menu`, `public/menu`).
- Never force-push `main`.
- Commit messages: 1–2 sentences, focused on why.
